 "body": [
  {
   "_key": "en",
   "_type": "object",
   "value": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000001",
     "_type": "block",
     "children": [
      {
       "_key": "79pncpr87ddg",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [
        "xfu91vdi18v9"
       ],
       "text": "Kom Ombo"
      },
      {
       "_key": "pq041sfnkft1",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": " Unforgettable Moments"
      }
     ],
     "markDefs": [
      {
       "_key": "xfu91vdi18v9",
       "_type": "internalLink",
       "reference": {
        "_ref": "wp-page-58875",
        "_type": "reference"
       }
      }
     ],
     "style": "h2"
    },
    {
     "_key": "000000000006",
     "_type": "block",
     "children": [
      {
       "_key": "000000000002",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": "The Kom Ombo Temple, nestled along the banks of the Nile in southern "
      },
      {
       "_key": "000000000004",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [
        "000000000003"
       ],
       "text": "Egypt"
      },
      {
       "_key": "000000000005",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": ", stands as a testament to the architectural ingenuity and religious duality that characterized ancient Egyptian civilization. This magnificent structure is a rarity among the myriad of temples scattered across the Egyptian landscape, primarily due to its distinctive design as a double temple. Dedicated to two deities – Sobek, the crocodile god of fertility and creator of the world, and Horus, the falcon-headed god of the sky – the temple embodies the harmonization of contrasting elements: water and sky, fertility and kingship, fierceness and protection."
      }
     ],
     "markDefs": [
      {
       "_key": "000000000003",
       "_type": "externalLink",
       "href": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Egypt",
       "newTab": true
      }
     ],
     "style": "normal"
    },
    {
     "_key": "00000000000b",
     "_type": "block",
     "children": [
      {
       "_key": "000000000007",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": "Dubbed both the “House of the Crocodile” and the “Castle of the Falcon,” the "
      },
      {
       "_key": "000000000009",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [
        "000000000008"
       ],
       "text": "temple’s"
      },
      {
       "_key": "00000000000a",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": " layout mirrors its dedication to these two gods. Its symmetrical design comprises two parallel sanctuaries, two entrances, and two interconnected yet distinct sets of chapels and halls, each side mirroring the other to honor its respective deity. This architectural duality is unparalleled elsewhere in Egypt, making Kom Ombo a unique destination for both scholars and travelers alike."
      }
     ],
     "markDefs": [
      {
       "_key": "000000000008",
       "_pendingInternalRef": {
        "sourceLocale": "en",
        "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/7-days-in-egypt-pyramids-temples-and-timeless-wonders/"
       },
       "_type": "externalLink",
       "href": "/7-days-in-egypt-pyramids-temples-and-timeless-wonders",
       "newTab": false
      }
     ],
     "style": "normal"
    },
    {
     "_key": "000000000010",
     "_type": "block",
     "children": [
      {
       "_key": "00000000000c",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": "The temple’s origins date back to the Ptolemaic dynasty, with constructions and enhancements occurring from the 2nd century BCE to the 1st century CE. Despite suffering from natural wear and the hands of time, the "
      },
      {
       "_key": "00000000000e",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [
        "00000000000d"
       ],
       "text": "temple’s"
      },
      {
       "_key": "00000000000f",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": " ruins provide a fascinating insight into the religious practices and architectural advancements of the era. The presence of intricate reliefs depicting medical instruments and surgical procedures on its walls further underscores the temple’s uniqueness, offering a rare glimpse into the medical knowledge and practices of ancient Egypt."
      }
     ],
     "markDefs": [
      {
       "_key": "00000000000d",
       "_pendingInternalRef": {
        "sourceLocale": "en",
        "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/temples-of-time-day-tour-to-nubian-temples-from-aswan/"
       },
       "_type": "externalLink",
       "href": "/nubian-temples-day-tour-from-aswan",
       "newTab": false
      }
     ],
     "style": "normal"
    },
    {
     "_key": "000000000018",
     "_type": "block",
     "children": [
      {
       "_key": "000000000011",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": "Additionally, the temple complex hosts a Crocodile Museum, which features mummified crocodiles, paying homage to Sobek and "
      },
      {
       "_key": "000000000013",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [
        "000000000012"
       ],
       "text": "highlighting"
      },
      {
       "_key": "000000000014",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": " the reverence ancient Egyptians held for these creatures. This museum, along with the temple’s design and dedications, underscores the complex relationship between the "
      },
      {
       "_key": "000000000016",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [
        "000000000015"
       ],
       "text": "people of ancient Egypt"
      },
      {
       "_key": "000000000017",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": " and their environment, as well as their gods."
      }
     ],
     "markDefs": [
      {
       "_key": "000000000012",
       "_pendingInternalRef": {
        "sourceLocale": "en",
        "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/suez-travel-guide/highlights/"
       },
       "_type": "externalLink",
       "href": "/guide/suez",
       "newTab": false
      },
      {
       "_key": "000000000015",
       "_pendingInternalRef": {
        "sourceLocale": "en",
        "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/uncovering-siwa-heritage/"
       },
       "_type": "externalLink",
       "href": "/guide/siwa-oasis",
       "newTab": false
      }
     ],
     "style": "normal"
    },
    {
     "_key": "00000000001a",
     "_type": "block",
     "children": [
      {
       "_key": "000000000019",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": "Kom Ombo Temple’s unique dual dedication not only underscores the Egyptians’ advanced architectural skills and religious sentiments but also serves as a bridge between the past and present, inviting visitors to marvel at its grandeur and delve into the rich tapestry of Egyptian mythology and history. It is a site where the duality of ancient Egyptian deities is vividly encapsulated, offering an unparalleled glimpse into the civilization’s spiritual landscape."
      }
     ],
     "markDefs": [],
     "style": "blockquote"
    },
    {
     "_key": "00000000001b",
     "_pendingImage": "https://travel2egypt.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/GettyImages-157675568-5c3ee84246e0fb00016e5151.jpg",
     "_type": "image",
     "alt": [
      {
       "_key": "en",
       "value": "Ancient Pillars of Kom Omb"
      }
     ],
     "caption": [
      {
       "_key": "en",
       "value": "Twilight at Kom Ombo  The Hieroglyphs' Silent Stories Unveiled"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "_key": "es",
   "_type": "object",
   "value": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000001",
     "_type": "block",
     "children": [
      {
       "_key": "x85df71c8fwn",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": "Lo Mejor de "
      },
      {
       "_key": "8giivdx0ev5p",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [
        "7nm6lh5kreuc"
       ],
       "text": "Kom Ombo"
      },
      {
       "_key": "2q8noyowdi7n",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": " "
      }
     ],
     "markDefs": [
      {
       "_key": "7nm6lh5kreuc",
       "_type": "internalLink",
       "reference": {
        "_ref": "wp-page-58875",
        "_type": "reference"
       }
      }
     ],
     "style": "h2"
    },
    {
     "_key": "00000000000a",
     "_type": "block",
     "children": [
      {
       "_key": "000000000002",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": "El templo de Kom Ombo, situado a orillas del "
      },
      {
       "_key": "000000000004",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [
        "000000000003"
       ],
       "text": "Nilo"
      },
      {
       "_key": "000000000005",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": ", en el sur de Egipto, es un testimonio del ingenio arquitectónico y la dualidad religiosa que caracterizaron a la antigua civilización egipcia."
      },
      {
       "_key": "000000000006",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": "\n"
      },
      {
       "_key": "000000000007",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": "Esta magnífica estructura es una rareza entre la miríada de templos diseminados por el paisaje egipcio, debido principalmente a su distintivo diseño como templo doble."
      },
      {
       "_key": "000000000008",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": "\n"
      },
      {
       "_key": "000000000009",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": "Dedicado a dos deidades -Sobek, el dios cocodrilo de la fertilidad y creador del mundo, y Horus, el dios del cielo con cabeza de halcón-, el templo encarna la armonización de elementos contrastados: agua y cielo, fertilidad y realeza, ferocidad y protección."
      }
     ],
     "markDefs": [
      {
       "_key": "000000000003",
       "_pendingInternalRef": {
        "sourceLocale": "en",
        "wpUrl": "http://travel2egypt.org/es/guia-de-viaje-de-kom-ombo/fiestas-nilo/"
       },
       "_type": "externalLink",
       "href": "/es/guide/kom-ombo/fiestas-en-kom-ombo",
       "newTab": false
      }
     ],
     "style": "normal"
    },
    {
     "_key": "000000000016",
     "_type": "block",
     "children": [
      {
       "_key": "00000000000b",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": "Apodada tanto la «Casa "
      },
      {
       "_key": "00000000000d",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [
        "00000000000c"
       ],
       "text": "del Cocodrilo» como el «Castillo"
      },
      {
       "_key": "00000000000e",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": " del Halcón», la disposición del templo refleja su dedicación a estos dos dioses."
      },
      {
       "_key": "00000000000f",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": "\n"
      },
      {
       "_key": "000000000010",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": "Su diseño simétrico comprende dos santuarios paralelos, dos entradas y dos conjuntos interconectados pero distintos de capillas y salas, cada lado reflejando al otro para honrar a su deidad respectiva."
      },
      {
       "_key": "000000000011",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": "\n"
      },
      {
       "_key": "000000000012",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": "Esta dualidad arquitectónica no tiene parangón en ningún otro lugar de "
      },
      {
       "_key": "000000000014",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": "Egipto"
      },
      {
       "_key": "000000000015",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": ", lo que convierte a Kom Ombo en un destino único tanto para eruditos como para viajeros."
      }
     ],
     "markDefs": [
      {
       "_key": "00000000000c",
       "_pendingInternalRef": {
        "sourceLocale": "en",
        "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/es/guia-de-viaje-del-oasis-de-farafra/parque-nacional-del-desierto-blanco/"
       },
       "_type": "externalLink",
       "href": "/es/guide/farafra/parque-nacional-del-desierto-blanco",
       "newTab": false
      }
     ],
     "style": "normal"
    },
    {
     "_key": "000000000024",
     "_type": "block",
     "children": [
      {
       "_key": "000000000018",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [
        "000000000017"
       ],
       "text": "Los orígenes del templo"
      },
      {
       "_key": "000000000019",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": " se remontan a la dinastía ptolemaica, con construcciones y mejoras desde el siglo II a.C. hasta el siglo I de nuestra era."
      },
      {
       "_key": "00000000001a",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": "\n"
      },
      {
       "_key": "00000000001b",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": "A pesar del desgaste natural y del paso del tiempo, las ruinas del templo ofrecen una visión fascinante de las prácticas religiosas "
      },
      {
       "_key": "00000000001d",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [
        "00000000001c"
       ],
       "text": "y los"
      },
      {
       "_key": "00000000001e",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": " avances arquitectónicos de la época."
      },
      {
       "_key": "00000000001f",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": "\n"
      },
      {
       "_key": "000000000020",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": "La presencia de intrincados relieves que representan instrumentos médicos y procedimientos quirúrgicos en sus paredes subraya aún más la singularidad "
      },
      {
       "_key": "000000000022",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [
        "000000000021"
       ],
       "text": "del"
      },
      {
       "_key": "000000000023",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": " templo, ofreciendo una rara visión de los conocimientos y prácticas médicas del antiguo Egipto."
      }
     ],
     "markDefs": [
      {
       "_key": "000000000017",
       "_pendingInternalRef": {
        "sourceLocale": "en",
        "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/es/templos-del-tiempo-excursion-de-un-dia-a-los-templos-nubios-desde-asuan/"
       },
       "_type": "externalLink",
       "href": "/es/templos-nubios-desde-asuan-kalabsha-beit-el-wali-y-kertassi",
       "newTab": false
      },
      {
       "_key": "00000000001c",
       "_pendingInternalRef": {
        "sourceLocale": "en",
        "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/es/vacaciones-en-egipto-desde-canada-un-viaje-a-traves-del-tiempo-y-los-continentes/"
